            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What is the engineering standard for luxury estate driveway paving in Weston, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates excavates native soil 12 inches deep, places heavy stabilization fabric, and compacts an 8-inch processed gravel base with a 5-ton vibratory roller. Crews lay a 2-inch dense binder course followed by a 1.5-inch top coat of fine-aggregate hot-mix asphalt. Driveway perimeters are finished with hand-set Belgian block granite aprons and extruded Cape Cod berms tailored to Weston's architectural standards.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates construct structural fieldstone retaining walls in Weston, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates excavates a 36-to-42 inch deep trench below the frost line, pours a reinforced concrete footing or compacts a 12-inch gravel pad, and lays natural New England fieldstone. Masons install continuous 4-inch perforated drainage pipes encased in crushed stone and filter fabric behind the wall to eliminate hydrostatic pressure and prevent frost heave in Weston.</p>
